# Copy to .env.local and fill in from your Supabase project:
#   Project Settings -> Data API -> Project URL and anon/public key.
#
# The anon key is meant to be public — it identifies the project, not the
# caller. Row level security decides what it can reach, and the schema grants
# the anonymous role read access to nothing. Do not put the service_role key
# here: that one bypasses RLS entirely and must never reach a browser.
#
# With these unset the app runs on the bundled sample trip, so a fresh clone
# works with no setup at all.
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# For the attraction seeder only (scripts/seed-attractions.mjs), never the app.
#
# The service_role key bypasses row level security completely. Do not put it in
# this file or in .env.local: pass it on the command line for the one run that
# needs it, so it never sits on disk beside the app.
#
#   SUPABASE_URL=https://xxxx.supabase.co #   SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE=eyJhbGci... #   npm run seed:attractions
#
# Note it is not VITE_ prefixed, so Vite would not expose it to the browser
# even if it were set here. That is a backstop, not a reason to set it.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
